# Standards Bases de Données

## Principes généraux

- **Normalisation** : éviter la redondance (3NF minimum)
- **Indexes** : sur les colonnes WHERE, JOIN, ORDER BY fréquentes
- **Contraintes** : NOT NULL, UNIQUE, FK au niveau DB
- **Nommage** : snake_case, tables au pluriel, colonnes explicites

## Prisma (TypeScript)

### Schema

```prisma
// schema.prisma
generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

model User {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  email     String   @unique
  name      String
  role      Role     @default(USER)
  posts     Post[]
  createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @map("created_at")
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt @map("updated_at")

  @@map("users")
  @@index([email])
}

model Post {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  title     String
  content   String?
  published Boolean  @default(false)
  author    User     @relation(fields: [authorId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  authorId  String   @map("author_id")
  tags      Tag[]
  createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @map("created_at")

  @@map("posts")
  @@index([authorId])
  @@index([published, createdAt])
}

enum Role {
  USER
  ADMIN
}
```

### Queries optimisées

```typescript
// ✅ Select uniquement les champs nécessaires
const users = await prisma.user.findMany({
  select: {
    id: true,
    name: true,
    email: true,
  },
});

// ✅ Include pour relations (évite N+1)
const usersWithPosts = await prisma.user.findMany({
  include: {
    posts: {
      where: { published: true },
      take: 5,
      orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' },
    },
  },
});

// ✅ Transactions
const [user, post] = await prisma.$transaction([
  prisma.user.create({ data: userData }),
  prisma.post.create({ data: postData }),
]);

// ✅ Pagination cursor-based (performant)
const posts = await prisma.post.findMany({
  take: 10,
  skip: 1,
  cursor: { id: lastPostId },
  orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' },
});
```

## SQLAlchemy (Python)

### Models

```python
from sqlalchemy import Column, String, Boolean, ForeignKey, DateTime, Index
from sqlalchemy.orm import relationship
from sqlalchemy.sql import func

class User(Base):
    __tablename__ = "users"

    id = Column(String, primary_key=True, default=generate_cuid)
    email = Column(String, unique=True, nullable=False, index=True)
    name = Column(String, nullable=False)
    hashed_password = Column(String, nullable=False)
    is_active = Column(Boolean, default=True)
    created_at = Column(DateTime, server_default=func.now())
    updated_at = Column(DateTime, onupdate=func.now())

    posts = relationship("Post", back_populates="author", cascade="all, delete-orphan")

    __table_args__ = (
        Index("idx_users_email", "email"),
    )


class Post(Base):
    __tablename__ = "posts"

    id = Column(String, primary_key=True, default=generate_cuid)
    title = Column(String, nullable=False)
    content = Column(String)
    published = Column(Boolean, default=False)
    author_id = Column(String, ForeignKey("users.id", ondelete="CASCADE"), nullable=False)
    created_at = Column(DateTime, server_default=func.now())

    author = relationship("User", back_populates="posts")

    __table_args__ = (
        Index("idx_posts_author", "author_id"),
        Index("idx_posts_published_date", "published", "created_at"),
    )
```

### Queries

```python
# ✅ Eager loading (évite N+1)
users = session.query(User).options(
    joinedload(User.posts)
).all()

# ✅ Select colonnes spécifiques
from sqlalchemy import select

stmt = select(User.id, User.name, User.email).where(User.is_active == True)
results = session.execute(stmt).all()

# ✅ Pagination
def paginate(query, page: int, per_page: int):
    return query.offset((page - 1) * per_page).limit(per_page).all()
```

## Migrations

### Commandes Prisma

```bash
# Créer migration
npx prisma migrate dev --name add_user_role

# Appliquer en production
npx prisma migrate deploy

# Reset DB (dev only)
npx prisma migrate reset
```

### Commandes Alembic

```bash
# Créer migration
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add user role"

# Appliquer
alembic upgrade head

# Rollback
alembic downgrade -1
```

## SQL Best Practices

```sql
-- ✅ Index sur colonnes filtrées/triées
CREATE INDEX idx_posts_published_date ON posts(published, created_at DESC);

-- ✅ Éviter SELECT *
SELECT id, name, email FROM users WHERE is_active = true;

-- ✅ EXPLAIN pour analyser
EXPLAIN ANALYZE SELECT * FROM posts WHERE author_id = '123';

-- ✅ Pagination avec LIMIT/OFFSET
SELECT * FROM posts ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 20 OFFSET 40;

-- ❌ ÉVITER: N+1 queries, SELECT *, LIKE '%term%' sans index
```

## Checklist DB

- [ ] Indexes sur colonnes de recherche/tri fréquentes
- [ ] Contraintes FK avec ON DELETE approprié
- [ ] NOT NULL sur colonnes requises
- [ ] Migrations versionnées
- [ ] Pas de N+1 queries (eager loading)
- [ ] Transactions pour opérations multiples
- [ ] Connection pooling configuré
